%d          → Date
%level      → Log level
%X{key}     → MDC value
%logger     → Logger name(Class name)
%msg        → Log message
%n          → New line
%clr()      → for color(ANSI) NOT SUPPORTED FOR FILE LOGS

Error   -> It is used for non-recoverable error.
Warning -> It is used for recoverable error.
Info    -> It is used for audit purpose.
Debug   -> It is used for investigation.
Trace   -> It is used for detailed investigation.

Simple difference
1. SLF4J = API / Interface

SLF4J gives you the methods you use in your Java code:

log.info("Fetching account");
log.debug("Account ID: {}", id);
log.error("Something went wrong");

SLF4J basically says:

"Here is a standard way to write logs."

It does not necessarily decide where or how the log is printed.

2. Logback = Logging implementation

Logback actually does the work of:

Printing logs to the console
Writing logs to a file
Applying log levels
Formatting the output
Rolling log files

So Logback says:

"Give me the log message, and I will process it."

